{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.LinearMap.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.mubarMeasured_sign_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.mubarMeasured_sign_odd","kind":"theorem","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorExactCoefficient.lean#L260-L269","doc":"The measured candidate's **sign alternates as `(−1)^{A−1}`** (for `A ≥ 3`),\nmatching #4389's Milnor-parity sign law: `μ̄_A > 0 ↔ A` odd.  Honest arithmetic\nabout the measured sequence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.mubarMeasured_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.mubarMeasured_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":250,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorExactCoefficient.lean#L250-L258","doc":"The measured candidate is **nonzero for every A** — the *shape* of the exact\norder law (leading coefficient ≠ 0).  This is a fact about the extracted `μ̄`\nsequence; it becomes the exact law **only if** the candidate is proved to be the\ntrue leading coefficient (open, Route A).  So this does NOT discharge\n`MilnorExactOrderConjecture`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.mubarMeasured_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.mubarMeasured_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorExactCoefficient.lean#L240-L248","doc":"The measured candidate has the **`−2` consecutive ratio** observed in the data,\nfor `A ≥ 3`: `μ̄_{A+1} = −2·μ̄_A`.  Honest arithmetic about `mubarMeasured` — a\nproperty of the extracted sequence, not a claim about the true coefficient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.mubarMeasured","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.mubarMeasured","kind":"def","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorExactCoefficient.lean#L225-L232","doc":"**Measured leading-coefficient candidate** for the A-component Brunnian\nMarkov-trace deficit (#4480): `μ̄_A = (3/4)·(−2)^{A−3}`, over ℚ.  EMPIRICALLY\nEXTRACTED (Richardson `h→0`, relerr ≤ 8·10⁻⁷ at A ∈ {3,4,5,6}); the A=3 value\n`3/4` is additionally **proved** from #4471's Borromean closed form.  This is a\n*candidate* closed form for the trace-normalised leading coefficient, **not** a\nproof that it equals the true coefficient (that is the open Milnor μ̄(12…A) content,\nRoute A). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.leadingOrderMeasured6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.leadingOrderMeasured6","kind":"def","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorExactCoefficient.lean#L221-L223","doc":"Measured A=6 leading Milnor order (#4480 witness): `≈ 10.0005`, consistent with\n`2(6−1) = 10`.  MEASURED, not proved — recorded; no theorem asserts `= 10`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.leadingOrderMeasured5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.leadingOrderMeasured5","kind":"def","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorExactCoefficient.lean#L217-L219","doc":"Measured A=5 leading Milnor order (#4480 witness): `≈ 8.0005`, consistent with\n`2(5−1) = 8`.  MEASURED, not proved — recorded; no theorem asserts `= 8`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.cyclic_trace_group_commutator_rearrange","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.cyclic_trace_group_commutator_rearrange","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorExactCoefficient.lean#L170-L184","doc":"**The group commutator is NOT collapsed to `τ(1)` by cyclicity** — the\npositive counterpart that locates where the real coefficient lives.  For a\n**group** commutator `g·h·g⁻¹·h⁻¹` (built from ring units `g h : Aˣ`, as the\nHecke image of a pure-braid band-commutator word is), cyclicity gives only the\nconjugation rearrangement `τ(g·h·g⁻¹·h⁻¹) = τ(h·g⁻¹·h⁻¹·g)` — it does **not**\nreduce to `τ(1)`.  Contrast `CyclicTrace.commutator`, where the *ring* commutator\ncollapses to `0`.  This is why the physical Jones-trace deficit\n`τ(1) − τ(g·h·g⁻¹·h⁻¹)` is nonzero at order `2(A−1)` (the Milnor content) while\nthe Lie tower's trace vanishes identically. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.leading_coefficient_witness_is_uninformative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.leading_coefficient_witness_is_uninformative","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorExactCoefficient.lean#L159-L168","doc":"**#4471's lower-bound witness is uninformative for a cyclic trace.**  #4471's\n`HasOrder.trace` provides an `s` with `τ (V n) = h^k · s`.  For a cyclic trace the\nleft side is `0` (`cyclic_trace_kills_iterCommTower`), so the witness may be taken\n`s = 0`: the h-adic divisibility is achieved by the zero element and constrains\nthe leading coefficient not at all.  This is the precise sense in which the order\nlower bound does **not** upgrade to the exact law along Route B. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.cyclic_trace_kills_iterCommTower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.cyclic_trace_kills_iterCommTower","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorExactCoefficient.lean#L147-L157","doc":"**★ THE TRACE-CYCLICITY SUB-WALL (Route B, PROVED).**  For every cyclic\nMarkov trace `τ` and every level `n`, the trace of the length-`(n+2)`\nLie iterated-commutator tower **vanishes**:\n`τ (iterCommTower c (n+1)) = 0`.  The tower's top level is a ring commutator,\nwhich any cyclic trace kills.  Hence the leading Milnor coefficient μ̄_A cannot be\nextracted from #4471's Lie tower by applying the (cyclic) Markov trace — it is\nprovably annihilated. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.CyclicTrace.commutator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.CyclicTrace.commutator","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorExactCoefficient.lean#L141-L145","doc":"**A cyclic trace annihilates every ring commutator.**  This is the engine of\nthe sub-wall: `τ([x,y]) = τ(x·y) − τ(y·x) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.CyclicTrace.cyclic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.CyclicTrace.cyclic","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorExactCoefficient.lean#L139-L139","doc":"The trace (cyclicity) identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.CyclicTrace.toLin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.CyclicTrace.toLin","kind":"def","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorExactCoefficient.lean#L137-L137","doc":"The underlying R-linear functional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.CyclicTrace.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.CyclicTrace.mk","kind":"ctor","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorExactCoefficient.lean#L135-L135","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.CyclicTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.CyclicTrace","kind":"structure","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorExactCoefficient.lean#L133-L139","doc":"A **cyclic R-linear trace**: an R-linear functional `τ : A → R` satisfying the\ntrace identity `τ(x·y) = τ(y·x)`.  Every Markov trace on a Hecke algebra is one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.iterCommTower_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.iterCommTower_succ","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorExactCoefficient.lean#L120-L123","doc":"The tower at level `n+1` is a top-level ring commutator by definition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.iterCommTower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.iterCommTower","kind":"def","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorExactCoefficient.lean#L112-L118","doc":"**Left-normed iterated commutator tower** (restated from #4471).\n`V 0 = c 0`; `V (n+1) = [c (n+1), V n] = c(n+1)·V n − V n·c(n+1)` — the **ring\n(Lie) commutator**, the h-adic linearisation of the length-`(n+2)` Brunnian\ngroup-commutator word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.trace","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorExactCoefficient.lean#L97-L102","doc":"**Trace transfer** (restated from #4471): any R-linear functional maps an\nh-order-`k` element to a scalar divisible by `h^k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.HasOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MilnorExactCoefficient.HasOrder","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MilnorExactCoefficient.lean#L92-L95","doc":"`HasOrder h k x` (restated from #4471): `x` is `h^k` times something, `h`\ncentral via `algebraMap`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}